 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 519750,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "If the money factor for a lease is 0.000015625, what is the annual interest rate?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "3.75%"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The annual percentage rate (APR) is APR = 2400 × MF, where MF is the money factor of the lease and the APR is calculated as a decimal.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"{\\text{APR}} = 2400 \\times {\\text{0}}.{\\text{000015625}} = 3.75\\% \"></span></p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
